References: <E2CBC1A3-3D67-454F-BC57-DD7D03F4808F@fas.harvard.edu> <429A223F-C77D-48A1-AB71-19854C369ABF@Princeton.Edu>
Message-ID: <950D7371-09B5-4463-96EB-2650825E2632@Princeton.Edu>

After further investigations, it turns out that Andy's problem can  
also be handled in Zelig with a different syntax. :) Suppose your  
model is:

Y = X + T + e1
T = X + Z + e2

then, the formula would look like:

list("mu1" = Y ~ X + T, "mu2" = T ~ X + Z, "inst" = ~ X + Z)

The key is that you need to include both X and Z as instruments. The  
current docs are misleading and so we will fix the docs in the next  
version.

Best,
Kosuke

